  "$p4d256Comment": "P4.D256: `plants` add ledger rows (the item worn by the transfer owner — last worn in a chat that no longer exists — and by the unattributed row; another item's row that a delete must leave alone). Every row carries `ledger`, main's wardrobe_wear_stats after the case. The transfers pair has no `files` table (v4 creates it lazily on first access), so the PUT cases plant v4's generateDDL text for it (from fresh_schema.json, the D23 dump) ahead of the picture rows.",
  "$unifyComment": "Unification (`f5e953a3f`): the ledger plants are INSERT OR REPLACE — P4.D263 grew the shared wardrobe-transfers builder with two `wearRows` for item …00a1 (unattributed + c7…001), and the (…00a1, c7…001) plant collided on the UNIQUE `COALESCE` index; the case's own row now replaces the fixture's on both sides. The `files` DDL plants are IF NOT EXISTS for the same reason: P4.D263's builder now ensures `files` through v4's own `ensureCollection` (the same generateDDL text)."
}
